From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000005 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OrientCOMPASS <316423573+OrientCOMPASS@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Oct 2026 06:40:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] btif_av: passive-sink - do not INT-open against peers

Now that SEPs correctly advertise TSEP=SNK (patch 0004-avdt), phones and
Windows act as INT and push SET_CONFIG to us.  Our simultaneous active
BTA_AvOpen (stock N sink behavior) grabs the same SEP pair first; the
peer then sees our SEID in-use and enters a DISCOVER->ABORT loop
(btsnoop-proven with Z40: connect fails, Windows shows device unusable).

Standard headphones are pure acceptors: skip the active open for SINK
uuid on both CONNECT_REQ and PENDING paths.  The incoming ACP path
(conn_created -> config_ind -> str_opened) builds the scb and still
emits BTA_AV_OPEN_EVT so btif state machine and Java callbacks settle.
---
 btif/src/btif_av.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/btif/src/btif_av.c b/btif/src/btif_av.c
index 03ba842..2b7adc0 100644
--- a/btif/src/btif_av.c
+++ b/btif/src/btif_av.c
@@ -330,8 +330,22 @@ static BOOLEAN btif_av_state_idle_handler(btif_sm_event_t event, void *p_data)
              {
                  memcpy(&btif_av_cb.peer_bda, ((btif_av_connect_req_t*)p_data)->target_bda,
                                                                    sizeof(bt_bdaddr_t));
-                 BTA_AvOpen(btif_av_cb.peer_bda.address, btif_av_cb.bta_handle,
-                    TRUE, BTA_SEC_AUTHENTICATE, ((btif_av_connect_req_t*)p_data)->uuid);
+                 if (((btif_av_connect_req_t*)p_data)->uuid == UUID_SERVCLASS_AUDIO_SINK)
+                 {
+                     /* Passive-sink: phones/PCs act as INT and push SET_CONFIG
+                      * to our SNK SEPs.  Opening as INT simultaneously makes
+                      * both sides fight over the same SEP pair (btsnoop proof:
+                      * DISCOVER -> ABORT loop, Z40 connect fail).  Skip the
+                      * active open; the incoming ACP path (conn_created ->
+                      * config_ind -> str_opened) builds the scb and still
+                      * delivers BTA_AV_OPEN_EVT, so the state machine settles. */
+                     APPL_TRACE_DEBUG("btif_av: sink connect - passive ACP mode, waiting for incoming AVDTP");
+                 }
+                 else
+                 {
+                     BTA_AvOpen(btif_av_cb.peer_bda.address, btif_av_cb.bta_handle,
+                        TRUE, BTA_SEC_AUTHENTICATE, ((btif_av_connect_req_t*)p_data)->uuid);
+                 }
              }
              else if (event == BTA_AV_PENDING_EVT)
              {
@@ -343,8 +357,8 @@ static BOOLEAN btif_av_state_idle_handler(btif_sm_event_t event, void *p_data)
                   }
                   if (bt_av_sink_callbacks != NULL)
                   {
-                      BTA_AvOpen(btif_av_cb.peer_bda.address, btif_av_cb.bta_handle,
-                                 TRUE, BTA_SEC_AUTHENTICATE, UUID_SERVCLASS_AUDIO_SINK);
+                      /* passive sink (see CONNECT_REQ_EVT): never INT-open */
+                      APPL_TRACE_DEBUG("btif_av: pending sink - passive ACP mode");
                   }
              }
              btif_sm_change_state(btif_av_cb.sm_handle, BTIF_AV_STATE_OPENING);
